speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, in view of recent confirmation by Statistics Canada and Canada Manpower of sharply increased unemployment in Atlantic Canada over last year, in some instances one third greater, as in my own area; the urgent demand by the premiers of Nova Scotia and Prince Edward Island for assistance for unbearable electrical costs; and the federal government's announced intention to increase transportation costs in Atlantic Canada, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Malpeque (Mr. MacLean):
That the Prime Minister convene an emergency meeting of first ministers of the Atlantic provinces to deal in particular with the alarming situation in respect of seriously deepening unemployment, escalating electrical costs and impending transportation cost increases;
that this House instruct the Minister of Regional Economic Expansion to report within thirty days on the impact of the government restraint and anti-inflation programs which are creating increased regional disparity;
that the President of the Treasury Board be instructed to present a re-allocated program of government expenditure which recognizes the necessity of flexibility to assure that regional disparities will not continue to increase.
